  (floor
    (sentence "A native compiler claim is allowed only when the supported subset emits a loadable Hati table with parity proof, target assembly receipts exist for the supported metal planes, Form-native target object floors exist for macOS Mach-O, Windows PE/COFF x64, and Android ELF/aarch64, the Form-native Android ELF/aarch64 executable shape plus Linux/arm64 and Android adb stdout/stderr/exit receipts are proven, the Windows x64 PE/COFF object links into a loadable DLL, swaps behind the same recipe symbol, can be called through a cross-platform minimal bootstrap exe with host-boundary measurements, and the emitted fkwu C carrier builds on Windows through the local LLVM/clang oracle, native metal/emit target rows run four-way, third-party compilers/drivers/models are treated as oracle/sample sources, Form-native JIT runtime rows, lowered residual JIT rows, value-native JIT span rows, numeric conversion/transcendental rows, tensor emitter-as-recipe rows, measured oracle-learning choice samples run four-way on fkwu for the supported lanes, Mac+Android native receipt/package evidence is explicit about its carrier, and unsupported BML shapes or unproven transports are named before table emission.")
